   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# Suite PKG — The packages\n\nThe Python (`mbse.{{PACKAGE}}`) and TypeScript (`{{NPM}}`) packages are one library in two languages, and share one version: mbse-basis [PRI-031: the version is the contract](https://github.com/pitaman71/mbse-basis/blob/main/docs/PRINCIPLES.md#PRI-031).",
   "id": "c0"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "import { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { join, resolve } from \"node:path\";\n\nimport * as Package from \"../src/index.js\";\n\nimport { assert } from \"./support.js\";\n\nconst ROOT = resolve(\"../..\");",
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "c1"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "<a id=\"PKG-01\"></a>\n## PKG-01 · Both packages carry one version, and the package loads",
   "id": "c2"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "const python = /^version = \"([^\"]+)\"$/m.exec(readFileSync(join(ROOT, \"python3\", \"pyproject.toml\"), \"utf8\"))?.[1];\nconst typescript = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(ROOT, \"typescript5\", \"package.json\"), \"utf8\")).version;\nassert(python === typescript, `${python} ${typescript}`);\nassert(typeof Package === \"object\");",
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "c3"
  }
 ],
